    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d264">

                <pb facs="0503" n="441" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg441"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">J.C.S.
                    Files</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Note by the Secretaries of the Combined Chiefs of
                        Staff</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        C.C.S. 654/8</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quebec</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-12">12 September 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Basic Policies for the “Octagon” Conference</hi></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The Combined Chiefs of Staff have agreed<anchor n="1" xml:id="d264-f1"/>
                        on ail the basic policies for inclusion in the final <hi rendition="#small-caps">Octagon</hi>
                        report to the President and the Prime Minister, with one exception.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>This exception is as follows: <list>
                            <label><hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>.</label>
                            <item>The British Chiefs of Staff have proposed the following as
                                paragraph 6 (<hi rendition="#italic">i</hi>) of C.C.S. 654:<anchor n="2"
                                    xml:id="d264-f2"/>
                                <quote rend="blockquote">
                                    <p>“Reorient forces from the European Theater to the Pacific and
                                        Far East as a matter of highest priority, <hi
                                            rendition="#italic">having regard to other inescapable
                                            commitments</hi>, as soon as the German situation
                                        allows.”</p>
                                </quote></item>
                            <label><hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>.</label>
                            <item>The United States Chiefs of Staff have proposed that this
                                paragraph should read as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                                    <p>“Reorient forces from the European Theater to the Pacific and
                                        Far East, as a matter of highest priority, <hi
                                            rendition="#italic">having regard to other agreed
                                            commitments</hi>, as soon as the German situation
                                        allows.”</p>
                                </quote></item>
                        </list></item>
                    <pb facs="0504" n="442" xml:id="pg442"/>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>The decision of the Combined Chiefs of Staff on this wording is
                            requested.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d264-f3"/></item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. J. McFarland</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. T. Cornwall-Jones</hi>
                    </signed><lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Combined Secretariat</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d264-f1" n="1" xml:id="d264-f1-content">
                <p>By action taken informally and in their final meeting at Washington before the
                    Second Quebec Conference.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d264-f2" n="2" xml:id="d264-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg219">p. 219</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d264-f3" n="3" xml:id="d264-f3-content">
                <p>For the wording agreed upon by the Combined Chiefs of Staff at their 173d
                    Meeting, September 13, 1944, see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg322">p. 322</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
